# Project Context: Jamarket (Automotive SaaS Marketplace)

## Core Mission
Jamarket is a B2B2C SaaS platform designed to digitize small car dealerships. It connects professional sellers with private buyers through a streamlined interface, real-time communication, and inventory management.

## Functional Roadmap & Priorities
(P0: Critical, P1: Important, P2: Bonus).

### A. Front-Office (Public & Buyer)
- **[P0] Smart Search Engine**: Dynamic filtering (Brand, Model, Price, Mileage, Fuel type, Location).
- **[P0] Ad Display**: Detailed vehicle pages with optimized WebP galleries and technical specs.
- **[P1] Real-time Messaging**: Secure chat system using NestJS Gateways (WebSockets).
- **[P1] Favorites**: User-specific "wishlist" for bookmarked ads (Auth required).
- **[P2] Booking System**: Shared calendar for scheduling vehicle test drives.

### B. Seller Interface (Professional)
- **[P0] Stock Dashboard**: Overview of Live, Sold, and Draft listings.
- **[P0] Ad Management (CRUD)**: Form with multi-photo upload.
- **[P1] Lead Management**: Interface to track and reply to buyer inquiries with chat.
- **[P2] Analytics**: Views per ad, click-through rates (CTR).
- **[P2] Sales Reports**: Strategic data (yearly sales overview, filtering by vehicle range).

### C. Back-Office (Super-Admin)
- **[P0] User Management**: Banning fraudulent accounts and Role-Based Access Control (RBAC).
- **[P1] Admin Scopes**: Management of administrative action perimeters and permissions.
- **[P2] Visual Customization**: Configuration of color themes and UI component display modes.

## Technical Requirements for the Jury
- **Eco-conception**: Lazy loading for images + server-side compression (WebP).
- **Performance**: High Lighthouse scores and optimized DB queries via Prisma.
- **Security**: JWT-based Auth, Bcrypt hashing, and GDPR compliance (Right to be forgotten).
- **Tests**: Mandatory Unit/E2E tests for vital flows (Auth, CRUD, Search).

## Persona & Content Writing

When creating or modifying **user-oriented textual content**, the AI must **always consult `docs/persona.md` before writing**, ensuring that tone, vocabulary, and messaging are aligned with this document.

### When to apply this rule
- Homepage (hero section, taglines, introductions, trust arguments).
- Marketing or institutional copy (about page, footer, banners).
- Narrative labels (subtitles, section descriptions, explanatory empty states).
- Engaging microcopy (CTAs, welcome messages, onboarding text).
- Any content where **brand positioning** matters—not neutral technical labels (e.g., "Save", "Delete").

### Writing requirements
- **Language**: French, as in `docs/persona.md`.
- **Target audience**: Reflect Jamarket Auto—small local garage, used vehicles, repair, desire to increase visibility and simplify interactions with clients (online listings, messaging).
- **Tone**: Professional, accessible, reassuring; avoid corporate jargon or a generic startup tone.
- **Consistency**: Never contradict the persona; if in doubt, reread `docs/persona.md` rather than inventing a new positioning.

